# Production Architecture

Use this target architecture when making production-oriented decisions for NexusAI:

- Next.js and TypeScript for the web application.
- FastAPI for APIs and AI orchestration.
- PostgreSQL with pgvector for metadata and vector search.
- S3-compatible object storage for documents, images, audio, and generated speech.
- Redis for caching, rate limiting, and short background jobs.
- Temporal only after ingestion workflows require durable execution.
- Qdrant only after pgvector no longer meets measured retrieval requirements.
- Managed embedding and LLM APIs initially; use vLLM on dedicated NVIDIA infrastructure when self-hosting is justified.
- Whisper or a managed service for speech-to-text.
- Kokoro, Piper, or a managed neural voice provider for production text-to-speech.
- OpenTelemetry, Prometheus, and Grafana for traces, metrics, logs, and dashboards.
- GitHub Actions for CI/CD.
- Prefer managed containers; adopt Kubernetes only when traffic and team operations justify it.

Keep local development lightweight enough for a 16 GB Apple Silicon Mac. Treat production services as replaceable adapters and add them only when the relevant production requirement is being implemented.
